llm-mini-infer
Copyright 2026 The llm-mini-infer Authors

llm-mini-infer is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, above.

llm-mini-infer includes code adapted from other projects. Each file it adapted starts with its origin's copyright
notice and names the upstream file (a CUDA file in its opening comment). The origins:


vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache License, Version 2.0 (above)
Copyright contributors to the vLLM project

Adapted from vLLM v0.30.0 (commit ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607), and changed:
- llm_mini_infer/kernels/csrc/gdn_decode.cu: csrc/libtorch_stable/gdn/fused_gdn_decode_kernel.cu
- llm_mini_infer/kernels/csrc/gdn_mtp.cu: the helpers and the delta-rule update of the same kernel
- llm_mini_infer/kernels/cutlass/fp8_gemm_sm120.cuh:
  csrc/libtorch_stable/quantization/w8a8/cutlass/c3x/scaled_mm_blockwise_sm120_fp8_dispatch.cuh and
  csrc/libtorch_stable/cutlass_extensions/common.hpp
- llm_mini_infer/render/content_format.py: vllm/renderers/hf.py (the chat template's content format)
- llm_mini_infer/render/messages.py: vllm/entrypoints/chat_utils.py and vllm/renderers/hf.py (the chat messages'
  conversion and the system messages' consolidation)
- llm_mini_infer/engine/ipc.py: vllm/v1/serial_utils.py (the msgpack encoder and decoder)
- llm_mini_infer/runner/cuda/graphs.py: vllm/compilation/breakable_cudagraph.py
- llm_mini_infer/output/detokenizer.py: vllm/v1/engine/detokenizer.py
- llm_mini_infer/api/auth.py: vllm/entrypoints/serve/middleware/authenticate.py
- llm_mini_infer/runner/cuda/runner.py: vllm/v1/worker/utils.py (the startup check of free GPU memory)
- llm_mini_infer/metrics.py: vLLM's metric names, help texts and histogram buckets (vllm/v1/metrics/)

Adapted from vLLM v0.33.0 (commit 4ba787ec9959e566d3b587a796dff07673324da5), and changed:
- llm_mini_infer/output/tool_args.py: vllm/parser/gemma4.py and vllm/parser/qwen3.py (the argument converters),
  vllm/parser/engine/parser_engine.py and vllm/tool_parsers/utils.py (the arguments' typing by the tool's schema)
- llm_mini_infer/metrics.py: the tool-call parser counter's name, help text and labels (vllm/parser/metrics.py)
- llm_mini_infer/output/reasoning.py: the efforts (ReasoningEffort), the effort map's check
  (validate_reasoning_effort_map) and the template kwargs (map_reasoning_effort), from vllm/renderers/params.py and
  vllm/entrypoints/common/cli_args.py
- llm_mini_infer/vision/fetch.py: DownloadBudget, from MediaRequestDownloadBudget (vllm/connections.py)
- tests/data/tool_calls/parser_vectors.json, tests/data/reasoning/vectors.json: test vectors derived from vLLM's tests
  (tests/tool_parsers/test_gemma4_tool_parser.py, test_qwen3coder_tool_parser.py and common_tests.py) and its
  parsers' outputs, with cases of our own beside them
- tests/api/test_api_logprobs.py: the test's oracle, from the logprobs models of
  vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py, the response builder of chat_completion/serving.py and the
  byte-fallback correction of vllm/v1/engine/logprobs.py

The API's error texts, metric names and parser behaviours follow vLLM's, for compatibility.


Hugging Face transformers (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers), Apache License, Version 2.0 (above)

Adapted, and changed:
- llm_mini_infer/render/jinja_env.py: src/transformers/utils/chat_template_utils.py (the chat-template Jinja
  environment), transformers 5.18.0
  Copyright 2024 The HuggingFace Team. All rights reserved.
- llm_mini_infer/vision/qwen.py: smart_resize, from src/transformers/models/qwen2_vl/image_processing_qwen2_vl.py
  Copyright 2024 The Qwen team, Alibaba Group and the HuggingFace Inc. team. All rights reserved.
- llm_mini_infer/vision/gemma.py: get_aspect_ratio_preserving_size, from
  src/transformers/models/gemma4/image_processing_gemma4.py, transformers 5.17
  Copyright 2026 the HuggingFace Team. All rights reserved.
- llm_mini_infer/models/qwen3_5/vision.py: merge_order and interp_taps, from src/transformers/vision_utils.py
  (get_vision_position_ids, _interpolation_axis_taps_weights), transformers 5.17.0
  Copyright 2026 The HuggingFace Inc. team. All rights reserved.
- llm_mini_infer/models/gemma4/model.py, llm_mini_infer/models/gemma4/assistant.py: the proportional RoPE
  frequencies, from src/transformers/modeling_rope_utils.py (_compute_proportional_rope_parameters), transformers 5.17.0
  Copyright 2024 The HuggingFace Team. All rights reserved.


SGLang (https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang), Apache License, Version 2.0 (above)
Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team

Designs followed, with no code copied:
- llm_mini_infer/kernels/csrc/gdn_mtp.cu: the GDN speculative-decode verify of SGLang v0.5.22
  (python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/fla/gdn_replayssm_spec_decode.py), itself ported from ReplaySSM
  (https://github.com/Johnny-Liou/ReplaySSM, Apache License, Version 2.0)
- llm_mini_infer/kernels/cutlass/fp8_gemm_sm120.cuh: configuration 3's tile, SGLang's on SM120 for 128 < M <= 256
- llm_mini_infer/runner/cuda/graphs.py: the breakable CUDA-graph backend, captured without torch.compile
  (python/sglang/srt/model_executor/runner_backend/breakable_cuda_graph_backend.py); the code is vLLM's, above


NVIDIA CUTLASS (https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass), BSD 3-Clause License (below)
Copyright (c) 2017 - 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.

llm-mini-infer's FP8 GEMM library (llm_mini_infer/kernels/cutlass/) is compiled from CUTLASS's headers (CUTLASS 4.5,
as FlashInfer ships it), so the compiled library in llm-mini-infer's image contains CUTLASS code.


Gemma 4 (https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-31B-it), Apache License, Version 2.0 (above)

Model configuration files, unchanged, for the tests. google/gemma-4-31B-it's model card gives its licence as
Apache 2.0 (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/gemma_4_license), and so does RedHatAI/gemma-4-31B-it-FP8-block's:
- tests/data/gemma-4-31b-it.config.json, gemma-4-31b-it.generation_config.json,
  gemma-4-31b-it.processor_config.json, gemma-4-31b-it.tokenizer_config.json: google/gemma-4-31B-it at commit
  842da3794eaa0b77d5f08bae87a17459d91ff475
- tests/data/gemma-4-31b-it-fp8-block.config.json: config.json of RedHatAI/gemma-4-31B-it-FP8-block at commit
  d7242548c457ab4b45bd3adb8937f2659af4739d, sha256 f83680dca1680f7dcc507bc801549a99f5b4346aa3fdf2a48b549b782a8ca999


Helm (https://github.com/helm/helm), Apache License, Version 2.0 (above)
Copyright The Helm Authors

deploy/helm/llm-mini-infer/templates/_helpers.tpl and serviceaccount.yaml start from the chart scaffold of
`helm create`.


llm-mini-infer's image

The image holds third-party software beside llm-mini-infer, each under its own licence: its
/usr/share/doc/llm-mini-infer/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES (deploy/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES) says where each licence is, NVIDIA's
terms among them, and where the GPL and LGPL packages' sources are.

